A||N||5||FieroSTETZ||stranded away from home! help!||||1||
Z||000000||FieroSTETZ||08-11-2001||03:13 AM||||i am stuck 1700 miles from home, and my fiero is wiggin with an idle of 3000! engine has 6k on it, compression is 180 on all cylinders - error codes are 24, 32, 35 - what can i do to fix it! where should i start? one is the speed sensor (the one in the tranny? code 24) (32 is egr soething) (35 is unknown, cant find it anywhere!) help please! have access to an autoparts store and tools, what can i do!?<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.shawnrocks.com/Animation1.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||rodmcneill||08-11-2001||03:44 AM||||Code #35 is Idle Air Control. First thing I would check for is BIG vacuum leak. EGR tubes are notorious for cracking on the flange under the plennum. Good luck!||||reg||1
Z||000002||mrfiero||08-11-2001||04:07 AM||||I would say your EGR tube is cracked or one of the big vacuum lines that attach to the TB came loose (under plenum).<P>This would cause all 3 codes to set, so once it's fixed all ahould be well.  <P>I recently got these same 3 codes.....it was just a vacum leak.<P>I think you'll be fine to continue on home (if that's where you're headed)......highway driving shouldn't be bad.  You'll just need to turn it off at stoplights, etc.||||reg||1
Z||000003||FieroSTETZ||08-11-2001||04:13 AM||||cool, will try that in the morning - if i take off the intake plenum to undo the egr valve (will block the hole on the bottom of the plenum if need be) can i reuse the 3k mile gaskets that are on there?<P>thanks for the replies so far, will respond with results.||||reg||1
Z||000004||FieroSTETZ||08-11-2001||04:14 AM||||oh, also, if i rev, the rpm's come back VERY slowly, does this fall in with the other symptoms?||||reg||1
Z||000005||mrfiero||08-11-2001||12:19 PM||||You can reuse the gaskets as long as they are still in one piece.<P>As for the idle.....what do you mean by the RPMs coming back slowly?   If the EGR tube is cracked or if their was a vacuum leak causing a 3000RPM idle then it will be instantaneous.  If the idle starts out normal then gradually gets higher then there may be another problem.<P>D'oh....I just re-read what you wrote.  If you rev it with a huge vacuum leak (i.e. cracked EGR tube) then the RPMs will take awhile to settle back down.<p>[This message has been edited by mrfiero (edited 08-11-2001).]||||reg||1
